**How to implement.** PTB's optical-constants records are read by the module that reads every other optical-constants file, so the adapter of step 455 parses nothing itself (001 §D 'PTB OCDB (CC BY 4.0): EUV / VUV n, k with uncertainties'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). The format is the one PTB publishes (`github.com/PTB-SR/ocdb`, branch `master`, `ocdb/db/data/<name>.txt`, verified 2026-11-04): `#` comment lines, among them `# n = (1-delta) - (i*beta)` and `# The values are provided with their 3-sigma uncertainty bounds. HB: Higher Bound. LB: Lower Bound.`, then the column header `#lambda/nm\t1-delta\tbeta\t1-delta_LB\t1-delta_HB\tbeta_LB\tbeta_HB`, then tab-separated rows, the wavelength in nm. The bounds are absolute values at the stated sigma level, not offsets. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs`: (1) `ImportError` gains `MalformedSourceFileErr of reason : string`, and its `describe` (step 445) renders `the source file is malformed: <reason>`. (2) The entry assembly of the tabulated import (`entryFromTabulated`, step 2: one isotropic dispersive segment over the table's `sampleRange` whose axis is `TabulatedNK table`, no magnetic or active part, a minted `MaterialId`) MOVES into `type TabulatedNkTable with member this.isotropicEntry (name : EntryName) (category : CategoryId) (description : EntryDescription) : MaterialEntry`, which `entryFromTabulated` calls, so the refractiveindex.info and CSV imports keep every field and number and one assembly serves every tabulated source. (3) `PtbOcdbText of string` with `.value`, the text of one PTB record. `type PtbOcdbText with`: (a) `member this.headlineOpt : EntryCitation option`, the text of the first comment line with its `#` and surrounding white space removed, `None` for a text without one; (b) `member this.importMaterial : Result<MaterialEntry, ImportError>`, reading the lines (`\r\n` as `\n`): the column header is the comment whose text after `#` starts with `lambda/nm`, its columns split on tabs and spaces; the sigma level is the integer before `-sigma` in a comment (ordinal, ignoring case), as `3` in `3-sigma`; every other non-empty line is a row of numbers split on tabs and spaces and read with the invariant culture. The columns `lambda/nm`, `1-delta` and `beta` MUST be present; the four bound columns `1-delta_LB`, `1-delta_HB`, `beta_LB` and `beta_HB` are all present or all absent. n is `1-delta`, k is `beta` (PTB writes n = (1 − δ) − iβ with β ≥ 0, the engine n + ik with k ≥ 0), and each wavelength goes through `toMeters Nanometer` (the one Units seam, `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Units.fs:75`). With bounds, σn = (n_HB − n_LB) / (2 × level) and σk = (k_HB − k_LB) / (2 × level): half the bound interval, divided by its sigma level. The rows are sorted by wavelength, their uncertainties with them, as `entryFromTabulated` sorts its rows (step 2); the table is `TabulatedNkTable.tryCreate` then, with bounds, `withUncertainty` (step 453), each `TabulatedTableError` answering `MalformedSourceFileErr` carrying its reason. The answer is `table.isotropicEntry (EntryName "Imported (PTB OCDB)") CategoryIds.semiconductor (EntryDescription "Imported tabulated n,k (PTB OCDB).")`, the category the tabulated refractiveindex.info import files (`MaterialImport.fs:502`), so the adapter names it (step 455). A missing required column, a partial set of bound columns, bounds without a sigma level, and a row whose value count is not the header's or that does not read are `MalformedSourceFileErr` naming the column, the level or the 1-based line; a text without a row is `NoDataErr`; every .NET call that throws is caught and answered `MalformedSourceFileErr`. No unit heuristic, second format or option is added. (4) Fixture: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/fixtures/ptb-Co.txt`, a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `fixtures/sample-nk.csv`'s with no comment: the seven header lines of PTB's `Co.txt` exactly (`# Optical constants for Co created by PTB`, `# Reconstructed from reflection measurements in the wavelength range 8 - 25 nm`, `# 40 nm Co thin film in a multilayer on Si (C/ Co/ Ru/ Si) (measured 4/2022)`, `# n = (1-delta) - (i*beta)`, the 3-sigma line, the column header and `# ------------------------`) and three of its rows, tab-separated: `8.0 0.96788 0.02267 0.96772 0.96804 0.02253 0.0228`, `11.2 0.95225 0.05349 0.95194 0.95256 0.05327 0.05371` and `25.0 0.92771 0.10418 0.92583 0.92962 0.10319 0.10517`; CC BY 4.0 data credited by its own first line. (5) Tests, in `MaterialImportTests`: `a PTB OCDB record reads n as 1 - delta and k as beta, its 3-sigma bounds as one-sigma uncertainties`: `(PtbOcdbText <fixtures/ptb-Co.txt>).importMaterial` answers one isotropic dispersive segment whose `TabulatedNK` table holds 8.0, 11.2 and 25.0 nm in metres, n 0.96788, 0.95225 and 0.92771, k 0.02267, 0.05349 and 0.10418, and σn and σk the fact computes from the row's bounds as (HB − LB) / 6 (within 1e-15); and `headlineOpt` is `Optical constants for Co created by PTB`. `a PTB OCDB record without bounds has no uncertainty, and a malformed record is refused`: a test-local text of the header without bound columns and two rows answers `uncertaintyOpt = None`; texts without the `beta` column, with `beta_LB` alone, with bounds but no sigma line, and with a row of six values each answer `MalformedSourceFileErr`; and a header without a row answers `NoDataErr`. `every import error renders its condition and its payload` (step 445) also renders `MalformedSourceFileErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the reader lands, `PtbOcdbText.importMaterial` MUST read a PTB OCDB record into one isotropic tabulated segment whose n is 1 − δ, k is β and per-sample uncertainty is the bound interval over twice its sigma level, and every tabulated import MUST assemble its entry through `TabulatedNkTable.isotropicEntry` with its fields unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a PTB OCDB record reads n as 1 - delta and k as beta, its 3-sigma bounds as one-sigma uncertainties`, `a PTB OCDB record without bounds has no uncertainty, and a malformed record is refused` and the widened `every import error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2; kit-acceptance MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests with AT-1 and AT-2 expectations and tolerances unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s44 invariants MUST pass.
